      "writtenOn": "2023-06-07T13:10:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not clear what \"above\" is referring to here.\nIn the source code, \"above\" was referring to this statement:\n\n```\n// approx_scale(x,y) approximates div255(cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(x)*cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(y)) within a bit,\n// and is always perfect when x or y is 0 or 255.\n```\n\nWe could just rephrase this? Maybe a bit verbose, but there\u0027s a lot to unpack here.\n\n```\n// All of (x*y+x)/256, (x*y+y)/256, and (x*y+255)/256 are good approximations\n// of div255_accurate(x*y). They are accurate +/- 1 bit of error, and are always\n// perfect when x or y is 0 or 255.\n```",
